WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.210
- Progress in the sexual
abuse case against

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:04.390
Prince Andrew of the Royal Family.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:05.640
As you may know, Virginia Giuffre

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.450
has accused Prince Andrew
of abusing her as a minor

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.380
in connection with Jeffrey Epstein.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.240
So she has been trying to personally serve

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.730
Prince Andrew with the
lawsuit papers so that

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:19.340
she can continue in her
lawsuit in New York.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.480
And not surprisingly,

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.470
Prince Andrew has been dodging service.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.410
You probably know that
when you file a lawsuit,

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:27.660
you need to usually personally
hand the service papers

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.050
to the defendant before you
can begin the lawsuit itself.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.320
And sometimes it's really
hard to serve people,

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.240
especially if they are evading service.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.110
In this particular case,

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:37.400
the court granted Giuffre's motion

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.730
for what's called alternative service,

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.300
saying that she had tried
everything to serve this guy,

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.560
but he's not making himself available.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.460
He almost certainly has
knowledge of this lawsuit,

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.240
so alternative means can be used.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.600
But in a twist, basically the day after,

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.140
Giuffre was able to
personally serve the Prince

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.170
at a private club in the UK.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:57.280
So, it looks like he's going
to be a part of this lawsuit

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.393
and we will see them in court.

